window.DOCSDATA={"docs":[{"id":"F01","title":"Active Service Letter Card, front, dated 26/7/44","html":"<p>Printed in blue (bilingual air-mail letter card, Union postal stationery with an imprinted 3d stamp):<br>ACTIVE SERVICE LETTER CARD · PAR AVION / BY AIR MAIL / PER LUGPOS · DIENS BRIEFKAART<br>\"If anything is enclosed, this Card will be sent by ordinary mail / As iets ingesluit word, sal hierdie kaart per gewone pos gestuur word\"<br>Imprinted stamp: <b>3D SOUTH AFRICA POSTAGE</b> (landscape design), with a circular postmark across it [date illegible].<br>\"When folded, the Letter Card must conform in size and shape to the blue border, within which the address only may be written / Wanneer gevou, moet die Briefkaart die grootte en vorm van die blou rand hê, waarin alleenlik die adres geskryf moet word.\"</p>\n<p>Handwritten in ink, in the address panel:<br><b>L/Cpl A.M. Lapinsky, No 176073(V)</b><br><b>S.A.M.C. Wing,</b><br><b>Administration H.Q.,</b><br><b>U.D.F.</b><br><b>MIDDLE EAST FORCES.</b><br>Left margin, written vertically in ink: <b>26/7/44</b></p>\n<p>Notes: the address panel names him as the addressee, at the S.A.M.C. Wing of Administration H.Q., U.D.F., M.E.F. — the postal address in use while he was on the S.A.M.C. General List and at the Transit Camp (9 Jul – 8 Aug 1944), eleven days before he emplaned for the Union. Only the address side of the card is reproduced here. The family remembers the card as part of his correspondence with his future wife. The card is torn at the top edge; a piece of the stamp panel is missing.</p>"},{"id":"F02","title":"Union Defence Forces medal transmittal slip (with the medals, 1957)","html":"<p>[Union coat of arms]<br>UNION DEFENCE FORCES.<br><i>The Chief of the General Staff has the honour to transmit, with his compliments, the enclosed award(s) for service during the war of 1939-1945.</i></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Order in which the Awards should be set up, e.g., for framing.</th><th>Description of Ribbon.</th><th>Clasp or Emblem (if awarded)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1 1939-45 Star <b>X</b></td><td>Dark blue, red and light blue in three equal vertical stripes. This ribbon is worn with the dark blue stripe furthest from the left shoulder.</td><td>Battle of Britain</td></tr><tr><td>2 Atlantic Star</td><td>Blue, white and sea green shaded and watered. This ribbon is worn with the blue edge furthest from the left shoulder.</td><td>Air Crew Europe or France and Germany</td></tr><tr><td>3 Air Crew Europe Star</td><td>Light blue with black edges and in addition a narrow yellow stripe on either side.</td><td>Atlantic or France and Germany</td></tr><tr><td>4 Africa Star <b>X</b></td><td>Pale buff, with a central vertical red stripe and two narrower stripes, one dark blue, and the other light blue. This ribbon is worn with the dark blue stripe furthest from the left shoulder.</td><td>8th Army <b>X</b> or <s>1st Army or North Africa 1942-43</s></td></tr><tr><td>5 Pacific Star</td><td>Dark green with red edges, a central yellow stripe, and two narrow stripes, one dark blue and the other light blue. This ribbon is worn with the dark blue stripe furthest from the left shoulder</td><td>Burma</td></tr><tr><td>6 Burma Star</td><td>Dark blue with a central red stripe and in addition two orange stripes.</td><td>Pacific</td></tr><tr><td>7 Italy Star</td><td>Five vertical stripes of equal width, one in red at either edge and one in green at the centre, the two intervening stripes being in white.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>8 France and Germany Star</td><td>Five vertical stripes of equal width, one in blue at either edge and one in red at the centre, the two intervening stripes being in white.</td><td>Atlantic</td></tr><tr><td>9 Defence Medal <b>X</b></td><td>Flame coloured with green edges, upon each of which is a narrow black stripe.</td><td>Silver laurel leaves (King's Commendation for brave conduct. Civil)</td></tr><tr><td>10 War Medal, 1939-45 <b>X</b></td><td>A narrow central red stripe with a narrow white stripe on either side. A broad red stripe at either edge, and two intervening stripes in blue.</td><td>Oak leaf</td></tr><tr><td>11 Africa Service Medal <b>X</b></td><td>Orange in colour with green and gold of the Springbok Colours in vertical stripes on either side. The green stripes being on the outside.</td><td>Protea</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>NUMBER OF STARS, MEDALS, CLASPS or EMBLEMS ENCLOSED. <b>6</b> (ink)</p>\n<p>A small white label top right carries <b>222</b> [?] in ink (later, not original). The five awards ticked match the file's entitlement stamp (P-1) and the discharge card (S-5); \"6\" = five medals plus the 8th Army clasp. The slip is undated; the medals were despatched on 1 March 1957 (S-5).</p>"},{"id":"F03","title":"Framed medal group with portrait","html":"<p>Blue mount in a gilt frame. Contents, as displayed:</p>\n<ul><li>Top: ribbon bar of five ribbons, in order 1939-45 Star, Africa Star (with the silver \"8\" of the 8th Army clasp), Defence Medal, War Medal 1939-45, Africa Service Medal.</li><li>Below it: S.A.M.C. cap badge (gilt crown over the rod of Asclepius within a laurel wreath, blue-enamelled scroll).</li><li>Left column: <b>Defence Medal</b> (above), <b>1939-45 Star</b> (below). Right column: <b>War Medal 1939-45</b> (above), <b>Africa Service Medal</b> (below, showing the map-of-Africa reverse).</li><li>Centre: studio portrait, sepia, head and shoulders, in battledress blouse; round spectacles and moustache; no rank chevrons visible; a light-coloured tab on the left shoulder strap [possibly the red \"Africa Service\" tab]. Undated.</li><li>Plaque: <b>AUBREY MITCHELL LAPINSKY / WORLD WAR 2 / 1939-1944</b> (the dates on the plaque differ from the file, which runs to his discharge on 24 August 1945).</li><li><b>The Africa Star is absent</b>: the family records that it went missing in the post. Its 8th Army clasp is represented only on the ribbon bar.</li></ul>\n<p>Note (2026-10-23): the \"Mrs A. Lapinsky\" named as next of kin on 19 August 1944 (S-5) is Ada Lapinsky, née Kimmel, the user's grandmother.</p>"},{"id":"P01","title":"File cover (brown folder)","html":"<p><b>176073</b> (top centre, underlined)</p>\n<p><b>L/Cpl</b> (top left) <b>LAPINSKY, A.M.</b> (underlined) <b>SAMC</b></p>\n<pre class=\"stampblock\">[STAMP:]  FINALISED\n            1939-45 STAR\n            AFRICA STAR AND 8 CLASP\n            DEFENCE MEDAL\n            THE WAR MEDAL (1939-45)\n            AFRICA SERVICE MEDAL</pre>\n<pre class=\"stampblock\">[STAMP, bottom left, Afrikaans:]\n  AANSPRAAK BEVESTIG EN\n  MLYS NA S.A. MUNT GE-\n  STUUR VIR GRAVERING.\n  VOLGNO. ....  6867  (handwritten)</pre>\n<p>(= \"Claim confirmed and list sent to S.A. Mint for engraving. Serial no. 6867\")</p>\n<p><code>[STAMP, bottom right, boxed:] DATE DISPATCHED / DATUM VAN VERSENDING</code> with date stamp <b>[2?]1-3-1957</b></p>\n<p><b>176073</b> (bottom right). Faint pencil <b>4m</b> [?] bottom left.</p>"},{"id":"P02","title":"D.D. 732 — Record Card (front), Middle East copy","html":"<p>(Buff card, red diagonal cancellation line across the whole card.)</p>\n<p><code>[STAMP, purple, top left:] REGISTERED AS VOTER   REF: </code> <b>18/1/10/41</b> [?] · pencil <b>176073</b> · D.D. 732.<br>Red pencil, diagonal: <b>FILE</b><br>CARD No. / No. van KAART: — · pencil above: <b>Disch auth 19/7/45</b><br>REGTL. No. / REGTSNO. <b>176073</b> + red <b>V</b><br>Red ink (right): <b>Attested 23 July 40</b></p>\n<p>A. — Surname (a) / Van <b>LAPINSKY</b><br>Christian Names (a) / Voorname <b>AUBREY</b> <s>AUBERY</s> [struck, mis-spelt original] <b>MITCHELL</b><br>Rank (b) / Rang: pencil <b>Pte</b>, with <b>T/L/Cpl</b> written above<br>Unit (b) / Eenheid: pencil <b>10/11</b> [over faint erased] <b>FIELD AMBULANCE</b>; below, faint pencil: <b>Left Union June 41</b><br>Date of Birth / Datum van geboorte <b>15-12-1918</b><br>Religious Denomination / Kerkverband <b>JEW</b><br>Next of Kin / Naasbestaande — Relationship <b>FATHER</b> · Name <b>MR. NATHAN LAPINSKY</b> · Address <b>24 ALEXANDRA AVENUE, BLOEMFONTEIN</b><br>Left margin, pencil: <b>No SB</b> [?]</p>\n<p>To be completed in RED INK. / Moet met ROOI INK ingevul word.<br>B. — Date record returned O. i/c War Records / Datum wanneer teruggestuur na die offisier vir oorlogsregisters: <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: 16-8-1944</span> · <code>[STAMP:] OFFICER i/c RECORDS, SECT. \"G\" · 2nd Echelon, U.D.F., M.E.F.</code> [signature] <b>Brownbill</b> [?] <b>Captain</b><br>Reason / Rede: red ink, capitals: <b>EMPLANED FOR UNION ON HOME EXCHANGE</b></p>\n<p>(a) To be entered in BLOCK CAPITALS. (b) To be entered in black pencil. [bilingual footnotes]</p>"},{"id":"P03","title":"D.D. 732 — Record of Service / Diensstaat (reverse of P-2)","html":"<p>RECORD OF SERVICE. — DIENSSTAAT.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Date / Datum</th><th>Nature of Casualty (Promotions, Punishments, Leave of Absence, Transfers, Postings, etc.) / Aard van verlies</th><th>Reference / Verwysing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>21 JUN 41</b></td><td><span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: DISEMBARKED SUEZ</span></td><td><span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: P.T. II O</span> <b>1 30/6/41</b></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><b>Granted local leave + 2/- p.d. ration allce. period 6/2/42 to 13/2/42</b></td><td><b>P.II O 7 23.2.42.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>23 July 41</b></td><td><b>Granted 4d p.d. annual increment</b></td><td><b>P.II.O. 5 4.8.41.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>3 July 42</b></td><td><b>Off strength — placed on S.A.M.C. gen. list</b></td><td><b>16 F.A. P.II O 24 13.7.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>On \" 16 Fd Ambulance</b> [i.e. taken on (General List) strength from 16 Fd Amb]</td><td><b>GL \" 27 \"</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>1-8-42</b></td><td><b>Detached to 10/11 Fd. Amb</b></td><td><b>— 31 10.8.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>2.9.42</b></td><td><b>On Posting to 10/11 Fd Amb from SAMC GL (10/11 FA 33/42)</b></td><td><b>GL 35 7.9.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>11.9.42 to 24.9.42</b></td><td><b>Granted leave + 2/- p.d. ration allce.</b></td><td><b>10/11 F.A. 35 <s>44</s> 21.9.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>19.10.42</b></td><td><b>Promoted to T/L/Cpl.</b></td><td><b>\" 40. 26.10.42.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>23.7.42</b></td><td><b>Granted 2nd annual increment of 4d p.d.</b></td><td><b>\" 44. 23.11.42.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>25 Jan 43</b></td><td><b>Admitted to hospital — on X2 list</b></td><td><b>\" 6 - 8 FEB 43.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>11 Feb 43</b></td><td><b>Disch. from hosp. + rejoined unit</b></td><td><b>\" 8 - 22 Feb 43</b></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>red ink: <b>P.Q. 113 to C.P. DR.O.P. 7/2</b> [?]</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><b>9 July 44</b></td><td><b>Placed on S.A.M.C. Gen List (G.L. O/29/44)</b></td><td><b>\" O/24/44. 17/7/44.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>6 Aug. 44</b></td><td><b>Emplaned for Union on Home Exch. SAMC</b></td><td><b>GL O/33: 14 Aug 44.</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Footer: 700 / PMEJ / 2 / 10.000—4/41</p>"},{"id":"P04","title":"Army Form B.122 (Conduct Sheet), 10/11 Field Ambulance (V), SAMC, UDF, MEF","html":"<p><code>[STAMP, header:] 10/11 FIELD AMBULANCE (V), SAMC, UDF, MEF.</code></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>Sqn., Batty., or Company</th><th>Corps</th><th>Date of enlistment</th><th>Sheet No.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>176073</b></td><td><b>Lapinsky A.M.</b></td><td>—</td><td><b>SAMC</b></td><td><b>23/7/40</b></td><td><b>1</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Date of last entry in Company Conduct Sheet: — · No. and date of last drunk: — · G.C. Badges: — · and G.C. Pay / Long Service: — · Signature O.C. Company etc.: —</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Place</th><th>Date of offence</th><th>Rank</th><th>Cases of Drunkenness</th><th>Offence</th><th>Names of Witnesses</th><th>Punishment Awarded</th><th>Date of award or of order dispensing with trial</th><th>By whom awarded</th><th>Remarks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><b>NIL</b> <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: 23 JAN 1943</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><b>CERTIFIED NO FURTHER ENTRIES</b> <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: - 6 JULY 1944</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>[signature illegible] <b>Capt</b> · Adjutant &amp; Q.M., <code>[STAMP:] 10/11 FIELD AMBULANCE (V), SAMC, UDF, MEF.</code></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>[P.T.O.] (Reverse side is blank; mirror-image show-through of the printed headings is visible.)</p>"},{"id":"P05","title":"Form DGD 15(A) — Record of Volunteer's Service (original, 2 pages)","html":"<p>(Typed pro-forma, entries in ink. Pencil number top centre <b>051264</b> [?]. Faint date stamp bottom right of P-5: <b>30-8-1945</b>.)</p>\n<p>FORM DGD 15(A)<br><b>RECORD OF VOLUNTEER'S SERVICE.</b></p>\n<p>SURNAME <b>LAPINSKY</b> CHRISTIAN NAMES <b>AUBREY MITCHELL</b><br>No. <b>176073V</b> Rank <b>Cpl</b> Married or Single <b>Married</b><br>Date and Place of Birth <b>15.12.1918 Durban</b> Age <b>26</b><br>Date of Assumption of Full Time Service <b>23.7.40</b><br>Date on Strength <b>14.8.45</b> R.O. No. <b>57/45</b><br>A.G. Authority/P.I. <b>WR(7) 176073V dd. 17.7.45</b><br>Reasons for Discharge or Release <b>Partial Demob</b><br>Was Discharge/Release with or without Benefits <b>With benefits</b><br>Immediate Grant Award (Brief details) <b>applied for bicycle + £228 for living expenses until qualified as an accountant</b><br>Applied for further Financial Assistance for [blank]<br>Referred to D.S.D.C. <b>Bloemfontein</b> date <b>23.8.45</b><br>Result if known <b>Not yet known</b><br>Pay in lieu of Leave granted <b>30 Days</b> and C.C.S.C.A. <b>£30</b><br>Identity Book No. <b>005778</b> Invalidity Badge No. <b>Nil</b><br>Total Period of A.W.O.L. <b>Nil</b> Period of Desertion <b>Nil</b><br>L.W.O.P. <b>Nil</b> Period of Effective Service <b>5 years 33 Days</b><br>Period spent in Civil Custody <b>Nil</b> In Detention <b>Nil</b><br>Conduct Assessment <b>Very Good</b> (blue ink)<br>Crime Record (Number of Crimes and Applicable M.D.C. Sections) <b>No Entries</b><br>Promotions and/or Reversions (with details and dates) <b>to L/Cpl Sept 42</b> [sic — other records: 19 Oct 42] · <b>To Cpl 1.1.45</b><br>Campaigns (with dates) <b>North Africa</b><br>Decorations and Medals (this war) <b>Africa Star with 8th Army Clasp + Africa Service</b> [Medal]<br>P.T.O.</p>\n<h4>page 2 (P-6)</h4>\n<p>Character Assessment <b>Very Good</b> (blue ink)<br>Medical Category — On Attestation <b>A1</b><br>On Discharge/Release <b>C</b><br>Nature of Disability if any <b>Dysentery</b><br>Date of Submission of Pensions Claim <b>13.8.45 Claimant</b><br>Result of Pensions Claim, if any <b>Not yet known</b><br>Hospitalisation (With particulars of ailments and dates) <b>25.1.43 to 11.2.43 Tonsilitis</b> [?, sic] <b>No 8 Gen Hos. Further Medical History not to hand</b><br>Pre-enlistment Employment <b>articled Clerk</b><br>Post-Discharge Employment <b>articled Clerk</b><br>Address of Employer <b>J.C. McIntyre Chartered Accountants, Bloemfontein</b><br>Residential or Home Address <b>14A Waverley Rd, Bloemfontein</b><br>Remarks [blank]<br>Date of Discharge <b>24.8.45</b> R.O. Order No <b>64/45</b><br>Forms Completed by [signature illegible] <b>Lt</b> [?] On <b>24/8/45</b><br>Checked by [signature illegible, over <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: O.C. DISP. DEPOT</span>] On <b>24/8/45</b><br>[signature illegible, blue ink] <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: O.C. DISP. DEPOT … CAPT</span> SIGNATURE OF DISCHARGING OFFICER.</p>"},{"id":"P06","title":"Form DGD 15(A) — Record of Volunteer's Service (original, 2 pages)","html":"<p>(Typed pro-forma, entries in ink. Pencil number top centre <b>051264</b> [?]. Faint date stamp bottom right of P-5: <b>30-8-1945</b>.)</p>\n<p>FORM DGD 15(A)<br><b>RECORD OF VOLUNTEER'S SERVICE.</b></p>\n<p>SURNAME <b>LAPINSKY</b> CHRISTIAN NAMES <b>AUBREY MITCHELL</b><br>No. <b>176073V</b> Rank <b>Cpl</b> Married or Single <b>Married</b><br>Date and Place of Birth <b>15.12.1918 Durban</b> Age <b>26</b><br>Date of Assumption of Full Time Service <b>23.7.40</b><br>Date on Strength <b>14.8.45</b> R.O. No. <b>57/45</b><br>A.G. Authority/P.I. <b>WR(7) 176073V dd. 17.7.45</b><br>Reasons for Discharge or Release <b>Partial Demob</b><br>Was Discharge/Release with or without Benefits <b>With benefits</b><br>Immediate Grant Award (Brief details) <b>applied for bicycle + £228 for living expenses until qualified as an accountant</b><br>Applied for further Financial Assistance for [blank]<br>Referred to D.S.D.C. <b>Bloemfontein</b> date <b>23.8.45</b><br>Result if known <b>Not yet known</b><br>Pay in lieu of Leave granted <b>30 Days</b> and C.C.S.C.A. <b>£30</b><br>Identity Book No. <b>005778</b> Invalidity Badge No. <b>Nil</b><br>Total Period of A.W.O.L. <b>Nil</b> Period of Desertion <b>Nil</b><br>L.W.O.P. <b>Nil</b> Period of Effective Service <b>5 years 33 Days</b><br>Period spent in Civil Custody <b>Nil</b> In Detention <b>Nil</b><br>Conduct Assessment <b>Very Good</b> (blue ink)<br>Crime Record (Number of Crimes and Applicable M.D.C. Sections) <b>No Entries</b><br>Promotions and/or Reversions (with details and dates) <b>to L/Cpl Sept 42</b> [sic — other records: 19 Oct 42] · <b>To Cpl 1.1.45</b><br>Campaigns (with dates) <b>North Africa</b><br>Decorations and Medals (this war) <b>Africa Star with 8th Army Clasp + Africa Service</b> [Medal]<br>P.T.O.</p>\n<h4>page 2 (P-6)</h4>\n<p>Character Assessment <b>Very Good</b> (blue ink)<br>Medical Category — On Attestation <b>A1</b><br>On Discharge/Release <b>C</b><br>Nature of Disability if any <b>Dysentery</b><br>Date of Submission of Pensions Claim <b>13.8.45 Claimant</b><br>Result of Pensions Claim, if any <b>Not yet known</b><br>Hospitalisation (With particulars of ailments and dates) <b>25.1.43 to 11.2.43 Tonsilitis</b> [?, sic] <b>No 8 Gen Hos. Further Medical History not to hand</b><br>Pre-enlistment Employment <b>articled Clerk</b><br>Post-Discharge Employment <b>articled Clerk</b><br>Address of Employer <b>J.C. McIntyre Chartered Accountants, Bloemfontein</b><br>Residential or Home Address <b>14A Waverley Rd, Bloemfontein</b><br>Remarks [blank]<br>Date of Discharge <b>24.8.45</b> R.O. Order No <b>64/45</b><br>Forms Completed by [signature illegible] <b>Lt</b> [?] On <b>24/8/45</b><br>Checked by [signature illegible, over <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: O.C. DISP. DEPOT</span>] On <b>24/8/45</b><br>[signature illegible, blue ink] <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: O.C. DISP. DEPOT … CAPT</span> SIGNATURE OF DISCHARGING OFFICER.</p>"},{"id":"P07","title":"Form DGD 15(A) — Record of Volunteer's Service (carbon duplicate)","html":"<p>Red pencil <b>3</b> top right. Content identical to P-5/P-6 except: \"Date on Strength <b>D 14.8.45</b>\" (an extra <b>D</b> before the date); the pencil number 051264 and the 30-8-1945 stamp are absent; the Invalidity Badge No. is left blank rather than \"Nil\"; the \"L/Cpl\" in Promotions is written \"<b>L/Cpl Sept 42</b>\". Signatures on page 2 are the same two officers as P-6.</p>"},{"id":"P08","title":"Form DGD 15(A) — Record of Volunteer's Service (carbon duplicate)","html":"<p>Red pencil <b>3</b> top right. Content identical to P-5/P-6 except: \"Date on Strength <b>D 14.8.45</b>\" (an extra <b>D</b> before the date); the pencil number 051264 and the 30-8-1945 stamp are absent; the Invalidity Badge No. is left blank rather than \"Nil\"; the \"L/Cpl\" in Promotions is written \"<b>L/Cpl Sept 42</b>\". Signatures on page 2 are the same two officers as P-6.</p>"},{"id":"P09","title":"Form D.G.D. III — Particulars of Discharge","html":"<p>(Typed form with handwritten entries. Red pencil <b>5</b> top right.)</p>\n<p>Payment in lieu of <b>30</b> days leave at date of discharge may be made.</p>\n<p>FORM D.G.D. III.<br><b>PARTICULARS OF DISCHARGE.</b> (For official use only.)</p>\n<p>No. <b>176073 V</b> Rank <b>L/Cpl</b> Surname <b>Lapinsky</b><br>Christian Names <b>Aubrey Mitchell</b><br>Attested at <b>Sonderwater</b> on <b>23 July</b> 194<b>0</b><br>For Unit or Corps <b>SAMC</b> at the age of <b>21</b> yrs.</p>\n<p>(i) For Europeans.<br>He is discharged in consequence of A.C.F. Regs. Chap. IV para 30<br>Section <b>WM. 58/43 as amnd. WM. 57/44 as amnd. WM 16/45 (E)</b><br>Reason <b>Partial Demobilisation</b><br><b>WR (7) 176073 V dd. 17/7/45</b></p>\n<p>(ii) For Cape Corps.<br>He is discharged in consequence of D.N.E.A.S. Regs. Section 47.<br>Reason ... <b>NIL</b></p>\n<p>The service he is allowed to reckon is <b>5</b> years <b>33</b> days.</p>\n<p>Character <b>Very Good</b> Education <b>Matric</b><br>Campaigns <b>North Africa</b><br>Identity Book No <b>005778</b><br>£30 civilian clothing and cash allowance <b>Paid</b><br>Discharged confirmed DISPERSAL DEPOT <b>TEMPE</b><br>Place <b>BLOEMFONTEIN</b> Date <b>24/8/45</b></p>\n<p><b>DESCRIPTION OF FINAL DISCHARGE.</b></p>\n<p>No. <b>176073 V</b> of the (Unit) <b>S.A.M.C.</b><br>Age <b>26 years</b> (Height) <b>5' 9\"</b><br>Complexion <b>Fair</b> Eyes <b>Brown</b><br>Hair <b>Black</b> Trade <b>Clerk</b><br>Distinctive Marks <b>Nil</b></p>\n<p>[signature illegible, blue ink] DISCHARGING OFFICER DISPERSAL DEPT <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: O.C. DISP. DEPOT</span><br>/LV.</p>"},{"id":"P10","title":"D.D. 872 — Details of Service","html":"<p>G.P.-S.40494—1945-6—75,000. S. · D.D. 872. · red pencil <b>22</b></p>\n<p>DEMOB. GROUP, ________ (To be completed in red ink or pencil.) [blank]</p>\n<p><b>DETAILS OF SERVICE.</b></p>\n<p>No. <b>176073 V</b> Rank <b>Cpl.</b> Name <b>Lapinsky A.M.</b><br>Med. Cat. <b>C</b> Date of Birth <b>15/12/1918</b><br>Corps <b>S.A.M.C.</b> Unit <b>140 Military Hospital</b><br>Place of Domicile prior to Enlistment <b>Bloemfontein</b><br>Married or Single <b>Married</b> Number of Dependants <b>1</b><br>Pre-Enlistment Occupation <b>Articled Clerk</b><br>Name and Address of Employer <b>J.C. McIntyre, Chartered Accountant, Bfn.</b><br>Any Special Training in U.D.F. <b>—</b> (e.g. Air Mechanic, Clerk, Wireless Operator, etc.)</p>\n<p>Date of Assumption of Duty for Pay Purposes <b>23/7/1940</b><br>Total Period L.W.O.P. <b>—</b><br>Total Period R.S.P. and/or Indefinite Release <b>—</b><br>Total Period A.W.O.L. (including confirmed desertion) <b>—</b><br>Total Period spent in Detention and/or Civil Custody <b>—</b><br>Period spent as P.O.W., if any <b>—</b><br>Sobriety [blank] Efficiency [blank]<br>Conduct/Character Assessment [blank]<br>Campaigns (showing Actual Unit Member served in) <b>Middle East and Syria.</b><br><b>16th Field Ambulance 3rd Bde. 2nd Division.</b><br><b>10th/11th Field Ambulance. 8th &amp; 9th Army.</b></p>\n<p>Decorations <b>Africa Star (8th Army Clasp). Africa Service Medal.</b></p>\n<p>REMARKS: <b>Has performed his clerical and medical duties to my entire satisfaction</b> (blue ink)</p>\n<p>[signature] <b>P.H. Sheldon</b> [?] <code>[STAMP:] MAJOR, S.A.M.C., OFFICER COMMANDING, MIL. HOSP., TEMPE.</code> Officer Commanding Unit.</p>"},{"id":"P11","title":"M.D.C. 46 — Conduct Sheet (Union copy)","html":"<p>G.P.-S.35033—1942-3—250,000. S. · M.D.C. 46.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>No. / No.</th><th>Name / Naam</th><th>Sqn., Batty. or Company / Esk., bty. of kompanjie</th><th>Corps / Korps</th><th>Date of Enlistment / Datum van diensneming</th><th>G.C. Badges / Onderskeidingstekens G.G.</th><th>Service or Proficiency Pay / Diens- of bekwaamheidsoldy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>176073V</b></td><td><b>Lapinsky A.M.</b></td><td>—</td><td><b>SAMC</b></td><td><b>19/7/40</b> [sic]</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Date of last entry in Company Conduct Sheet: — · No. and date of last drunk: — · Period not calculated towards exemption from extra fine: — · Sheet No. <b>1</b> · Signature of O.C. Coy.: — · Conduct: —</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Place</th><th>Date of Offence</th><th>Rank</th><th>Cases of Drunkenness</th><th>Offence / Oortreding</th><th>Names of Witnesses</th><th>Punishment Awarded</th><th>Date of Award or of Order dispensing with Trial</th><th>By whom awarded</th><th>Remarks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: CERTIFIED NO ENTRIES</span> <b>while at SAMC T/C</b> [?]</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>[signature illegible] <b>Capt</b> <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP:] OFFICER COMMANDING, S.A.M.C. TRAINING CENTRE<code> </code>[STAMP: 30 NOV 1944</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><b>Certified no further entries as at 13/8/45.</b> [signature illegible] <b>Lt/Capt</b> [?] <code>[STAMP:] MAJOR, S.A.M.C., OFFICER COMMANDING, MIL. HOSP. TEMPE</code></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"P12","title":"M.D.C. 46 — Conduct Sheet (Middle East copy)","html":"<p>§ G.P.-S.6548—1940—200,000. S. · M.D.C. 46.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>No. / No.</th><th>Name / Naam</th><th>Sqn., Batty. or Company / Esk., Bty. of Kompanjie</th><th>Corps / Korps</th><th>Date of Enlistment / Datum van indiensneming</th><th>G.C. Badges / Onderskeidingstekens G.G.</th><th>Service or Proficiency Pay / Diens- of bekwaamheidsoldy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>176073V</b></td><td><b>LAPINSKY A.M.</b></td><td>—</td><td><b>S.A.M.C.</b></td><td><b>19/7/40</b> [sic]</td><td>—</td><td><b>6d per day</b> (pencil)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Date of last entry in Company Conduct Sheet: — · No. and date of last drunk: — · Period not reckoning towards freedom from extra fine: — · Sheet No. <b>1</b> · Signature of O.C. Coy., etc. <b>H.I. Lewin (Lt.)</b> (pencil) · Conduct: <b>—</b> [illegible pencil mark]</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Place</th><th>Date of Offence</th><th>Rank</th><th>Cases of Drunkenness</th><th>Offence</th><th>Names of Witnesses</th><th>Punishment Awarded</th><th>Date of Award…</th><th>By whom awarded</th><th>Remarks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>pencil: <b>Offr i/c \"G\"</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><code>[STAMP, boxed:] CERTIFIED NO FURTHER ENTRIES · 2nd ECHELON U.D.F., M.E.F.</code> [signature] <b>Brownbill</b> [?] <b>Capt</b> · <b>6/8/44</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: CERTIFIED NO ENTRIES</span> <b>while at SAMC T/C</b> [?, reads \"S/C\"]</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>[signature illegible] <b>Capt</b> <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP:] OFFICER COMMANDING, S.A.M.C. TRAINING CENTRE<code> </code>[STAMP: 30 NOV 1944</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><b>Certified no further entries as at 13/8/45.</b> [signature] <b>Louis Cockell</b> [?] <b>Lt</b> [?] <code>[STAMP:] MAJOR, S.A.M.C., OFFICER COMMANDING, MIL. HOSP., TEMPE.</code></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(Note: P-11 is the Union-side copy of this same sheet, with the same two Union certifications but without the 2nd Echelon M.E.F. stamp.)</p>"},{"id":"P13","title":"D.D. 88 B — Attestation (Volunteer Units of the Union Defence Force)","html":"<p>G.P.-S.3481—1940—200,000. S. · D.D. 88 B. · pencil <b>1</b> top right · [Union coat of arms] · To be completed in duplicate.</p>\n<p>UNION OF SOUTH AFRICA.<br><b>VOLUNTEER UNITS OF THE UNION DEFENCE FORCE.</b><br>TO BE COMPLETED IN RESPECT OF VOLUNTEERS FOR SERVICE IN OR OUTSIDE SOUTH AFRICA.</p>\n<p>ATTESTATION OF<br>No. <b>176073.</b> Name <b>Lapinsky A.M.</b> Unit or Corps <b>S.A.M.C.</b></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Questions to be put before Attestation.</th><th>Answers.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1. What is your full name?</td><td><b>LAPINSKY AUBREY MITCHELL</b></td></tr><tr><td>2. Where were you born?</td><td><s>Jo'b</s> [struck] <b>Durban</b></td></tr><tr><td>3. What is your age? (Give date of Birth if possible)</td><td><b>21</b> years, <b>7</b> months. Date of Birth <b>15. 12. 18.</b></td></tr><tr><td>4. Nationality</td><td><b>Jewish</b></td></tr><tr><td>5. What is your trade or calling? (State if an indentured apprentice.)</td><td><b>Accountant</b></td></tr><tr><td>6. Do you now belong to any of His Majesty's Naval, Military or Air Forces, or the Union Defence Forces; If so, which?</td><td><b>S.A.C.S.</b></td></tr><tr><td>7. Have you ever served in any such forces? If so, state the particulars of your former service</td><td><b>One Year.</b></td></tr><tr><td>8. Have you ever been convicted by a Civil Court? If so, state crime and punishment</td><td><b>No</b></td></tr><tr><td>9. Are you married or single?</td><td><b>Single</b></td></tr><tr><td>10. If married, how many children have you? Give ages.</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>11. Who is your next-of-kin?</td><td>Relationship <b>Father.</b> Name <b>Mr. Nathan Lapinsky</b> Address <b>24 Alexandra Av. Bloemfontein.</b></td></tr><tr><td>12. Are you willing to be vaccinated or inoculated against infectious disease as occasion demands</td><td><b>Yes.</b></td></tr><tr><td>13. What is your private address?</td><td><b>24 Alexandra Av. Bloemfontein</b></td></tr><tr><td>14. Do you understand that if your period of engagement expires whilst you are employed on active service you will, in terms of Section 83 of the Defence Act, continue to serve until you are legally discharged?</td><td><b>Yes</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h4>reverse (P-14)</h4>\n<p>D.D. 88 B. · pencil <b>1</b></p>\n<p>I, <b>Aubrey Mitchell Lapinsky</b> do solemnly and sincerely declare that to the best of my knowledge and belief the above answers made by me to the above questions are true and that I am willing to fulfil the engagements made.</p>\n<p><b>H.G. Mowbe</b> [?] Witness. · <b>A.M. Lapinsky</b> Signature of Volunteer.</p>\n<p>OATH TO BE TAKEN ON ATTESTATION.</p>\n<p>I, <b>Aubrey Mitchell Lapinsky</b> *do make oath and say / <s>solemnly declare</s> that I will be faithful and bear true allegiance to his Majesty King George VI and to his heirs and successors according to law,</p>\n<p>that I will perform to the best of my ability the duties assigned to me as a volunteer member of the Union Defence Forces,</p>\n<p>that in accordance with the Resolution of Parliament I will serve in the *<s>South African Permanent Force</s>/<s>Coast Garrison Force</s>/Active Citizen Force in Africa whether within or outside of the limits of South Africa for the duration of the present War,</p>\n<p>that I subject myself, wherever I may be so serving, to the provisions of the South Africa Defence Act, 1912, as amended from time to time and to such rules and regulations as may be in force, or may from time to time be made and promulgated and are applicable to the *<s>South African Permanent Force</s>/<s>Coast Garrison Force</s>/Active Citizen Force, and to the Union Military Discipline Code.</p>\n<p>So Help me God.</p>\n<p>(Each deletion is initialled in the margin by both parties: <b>A.M.L.</b> and <b>H.G.M.</b> [?] — initials appear in the left margin beside the oath paragraphs, beside the \"Sworn/Declared\" line, and in the right margin and below the last paragraph.)</p>\n<p><b>A.M. Lapinsky</b> Signature of Volunteer. · <b>H.G. Mowbe</b> [?] Witness.</p>\n<p>*Sworn / <s>Declared</s> before me at <b>Sonderwater</b> this <b>23rd</b> day of <b>July</b> 194<b>0</b><br>[signature] <b>L.A. Denny</b> [?] Signature of Justice of the Peace <s>or Commissioner of Oaths</s>.</p>\n<p>Description of <b>A.M. Lapinsky</b> on attestation.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Age apparent <b>21</b></td><td>Complexion <b>Fair</b></td></tr><tr><td>Height (without boots) <b>5' 7\"</b></td><td>Eyes <b>Brown</b></td></tr><tr><td>Weight <b>136</b></td><td>Hair <b>Dark</b></td></tr><tr><td>Distinctive marks <b>Nil</b></td><td>Chest measurement (deflated) <b>33\"</b></td></tr><tr><td>Religious denomination <b>J.</b></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>* Delete whichever does not apply.</p>\n<p>(Note: no \"ANYWHERE\" stamp appears on this copy; the oath wording is the Africa Service oath — \"in Africa whether within or outside of the limits of South Africa\".)</p>"},{"id":"P14","title":"D.D. 88 B — Attestation (Volunteer Units of the Union Defence Force)","html":"<p>G.P.-S.3481—1940—200,000. S. · D.D. 88 B. · pencil <b>1</b> top right · [Union coat of arms] · To be completed in duplicate.</p>\n<p>UNION OF SOUTH AFRICA.<br><b>VOLUNTEER UNITS OF THE UNION DEFENCE FORCE.</b><br>TO BE COMPLETED IN RESPECT OF VOLUNTEERS FOR SERVICE IN OR OUTSIDE SOUTH AFRICA.</p>\n<p>ATTESTATION OF<br>No. <b>176073.</b> Name <b>Lapinsky A.M.</b> Unit or Corps <b>S.A.M.C.</b></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Questions to be put before Attestation.</th><th>Answers.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1. What is your full name?</td><td><b>LAPINSKY AUBREY MITCHELL</b></td></tr><tr><td>2. Where were you born?</td><td><s>Jo'b</s> [struck] <b>Durban</b></td></tr><tr><td>3. What is your age? (Give date of Birth if possible)</td><td><b>21</b> years, <b>7</b> months. Date of Birth <b>15. 12. 18.</b></td></tr><tr><td>4. Nationality</td><td><b>Jewish</b></td></tr><tr><td>5. What is your trade or calling? (State if an indentured apprentice.)</td><td><b>Accountant</b></td></tr><tr><td>6. Do you now belong to any of His Majesty's Naval, Military or Air Forces, or the Union Defence Forces; If so, which?</td><td><b>S.A.C.S.</b></td></tr><tr><td>7. Have you ever served in any such forces? If so, state the particulars of your former service</td><td><b>One Year.</b></td></tr><tr><td>8. Have you ever been convicted by a Civil Court? If so, state crime and punishment</td><td><b>No</b></td></tr><tr><td>9. Are you married or single?</td><td><b>Single</b></td></tr><tr><td>10. If married, how many children have you? Give ages.</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>11. Who is your next-of-kin?</td><td>Relationship <b>Father.</b> Name <b>Mr. Nathan Lapinsky</b> Address <b>24 Alexandra Av. Bloemfontein.</b></td></tr><tr><td>12. Are you willing to be vaccinated or inoculated against infectious disease as occasion demands</td><td><b>Yes.</b></td></tr><tr><td>13. What is your private address?</td><td><b>24 Alexandra Av. Bloemfontein</b></td></tr><tr><td>14. Do you understand that if your period of engagement expires whilst you are employed on active service you will, in terms of Section 83 of the Defence Act, continue to serve until you are legally discharged?</td><td><b>Yes</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h4>reverse (P-14)</h4>\n<p>D.D. 88 B. · pencil <b>1</b></p>\n<p>I, <b>Aubrey Mitchell Lapinsky</b> do solemnly and sincerely declare that to the best of my knowledge and belief the above answers made by me to the above questions are true and that I am willing to fulfil the engagements made.</p>\n<p><b>H.G. Mowbe</b> [?] Witness. · <b>A.M. Lapinsky</b> Signature of Volunteer.</p>\n<p>OATH TO BE TAKEN ON ATTESTATION.</p>\n<p>I, <b>Aubrey Mitchell Lapinsky</b> *do make oath and say / <s>solemnly declare</s> that I will be faithful and bear true allegiance to his Majesty King George VI and to his heirs and successors according to law,</p>\n<p>that I will perform to the best of my ability the duties assigned to me as a volunteer member of the Union Defence Forces,</p>\n<p>that in accordance with the Resolution of Parliament I will serve in the *<s>South African Permanent Force</s>/<s>Coast Garrison Force</s>/Active Citizen Force in Africa whether within or outside of the limits of South Africa for the duration of the present War,</p>\n<p>that I subject myself, wherever I may be so serving, to the provisions of the South Africa Defence Act, 1912, as amended from time to time and to such rules and regulations as may be in force, or may from time to time be made and promulgated and are applicable to the *<s>South African Permanent Force</s>/<s>Coast Garrison Force</s>/Active Citizen Force, and to the Union Military Discipline Code.</p>\n<p>So Help me God.</p>\n<p>(Each deletion is initialled in the margin by both parties: <b>A.M.L.</b> and <b>H.G.M.</b> [?] — initials appear in the left margin beside the oath paragraphs, beside the \"Sworn/Declared\" line, and in the right margin and below the last paragraph.)</p>\n<p><b>A.M. Lapinsky</b> Signature of Volunteer. · <b>H.G. Mowbe</b> [?] Witness.</p>\n<p>*Sworn / <s>Declared</s> before me at <b>Sonderwater</b> this <b>23rd</b> day of <b>July</b> 194<b>0</b><br>[signature] <b>L.A. Denny</b> [?] Signature of Justice of the Peace <s>or Commissioner of Oaths</s>.</p>\n<p>Description of <b>A.M. Lapinsky</b> on attestation.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Age apparent <b>21</b></td><td>Complexion <b>Fair</b></td></tr><tr><td>Height (without boots) <b>5' 7\"</b></td><td>Eyes <b>Brown</b></td></tr><tr><td>Weight <b>136</b></td><td>Hair <b>Dark</b></td></tr><tr><td>Distinctive marks <b>Nil</b></td><td>Chest measurement (deflated) <b>33\"</b></td></tr><tr><td>Religious denomination <b>J.</b></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>* Delete whichever does not apply.</p>\n<p>(Note: no \"ANYWHERE\" stamp appears on this copy; the oath wording is the Africa Service oath — \"in Africa whether within or outside of the limits of South Africa\".)</p>"},{"id":"P15","title":"Form D.G.D. III — Particulars of Discharge (duplicate; scanned upside-down)","html":"<p>Content identical to P-9 (same typing and handwriting, carbon duplicate), including: No. 176073 V, Rank L/Cpl, attested Sonderwater 23 July 1940, SAMC, age 21; Section WM. 58/43 as amnd. WM. 57/44 as amnd. WM 16/45 (E); Partial Demobilisation; WR (7) 176073 V dd. 17/7/45; service 5 years 33 days; Character Very Good; Education Matric; Campaigns North Africa; Identity Book No 005778; £30 allowance Paid; Dispersal Depot Tempe, Bloemfontein, 24/8/45; Description: age 26 years, height 5' 9\", complexion Fair, eyes Brown, hair Black, trade Clerk, distinctive marks Nil; same discharging officer's signature over <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: O.C. DISP. DEPOT</span>; \"/LV.\" No red page number on this copy.</p>"},{"id":"P16","title":"Form D.D. 873 — Application for Campaign Medals (1939 onwards) — front","html":"<p>G.P.-S.40432—1945-6—300,000. S. · FOR PERSONS DISCHARGED FROM U.D.F. · Form D.D. 873.<br>Pencil annotation top right: <b>Dismart</b> [?] (clerk's name; cf. \"Smart\" on P-18/19)</p>\n<p><b>APPLICATION FOR CAMPAIGN MEDALS (1939 onwards).</b></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>1939-45 Star</th><th>Atlantic Star</th><th>Air Crew Europe Star</th><th>Africa Star</th><th>Pacific Star</th><th>Burma Star</th><th>Italy Star</th><th>France and Germany Star</th><th>Defence Medal (British)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(ticked/boxed in blue pencil)</td><td></td><td></td><td><b>8</b> (boxed, blue pencil)</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>(boxed, blue pencil)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(The medals are shown in the order in which they will be worn.) Pencil: <b>L/Cpl</b></p>\n<p><b>A.</b> Surname (Mr., Mrs., Miss) <b>MR. LAPINSKY</b> Christian Names <b>AUBREY MITCHELL</b><br>Regtl. No. in U.D.F. <b>176073 V</b> (If you attested more than once, quote all regtl. numbers.)<br>Permanent Residential Address <b>14A WAVERLEY RD, BLOEMFONTEIN</b><br>(If you change your address after posting this application, please advise new address to which your ribbons should be posted.)</p>\n<p><b>B.</b> Date of attestation for full time service <b>23.7.40</b> Where did you attest <b>SONDERWATER</b><br>Date of commencement of full time service <b>23.7.40</b><br>To which Unit were you first posted on attestation <b>16th FIELD AMB (SAMC)</b><br>Give full details hereunder of your service in U.D.F.:—</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>SERVICES RENDERED WITHIN THE UNION — Name of Unit</th><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>SERVICES RENDERED OUTSIDE THE UNION — Name of Unit, Squadron, etc.</th><th>Name of Country</th><th>From</th><th>To</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>SAMC</b></td><td><b>23.7.40</b></td><td><b>26.7.40</b></td><td><b>16th FLD. AMBULANCE</b></td><td><b>EGYPT / CYRENNAICA</b> [sic]</td><td><b>10.6.41</b></td><td><b>20.6.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>16th Fld. Amb (SAMC)</b></td><td><b>27.7.40</b></td><td><b>9.6.41</b></td><td><b>8 C.C.S.</b></td><td><b>EGYPT</b></td><td><b>21.6.42</b></td><td><b>31.7.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>SAMC</b></td><td><b>10.8.44</b></td><td><b>12.10.44</b></td><td><b>10/11 FLD. AMB.</b></td><td><b>EGYPT</b></td><td><b>1/8/42</b></td><td><b>12/4/43</b></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><b>TRIPOLITANIA</b></td><td><b>13/4/43</b></td><td><b>30/11/43</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>140 Mil. Hosp. BLOEMFONTEIN (SAMC)</b></td><td><b>13.10.44</b></td><td><b>12.8.44</b> [sic — 12.8.45]</td><td></td><td><b>EGYPT</b></td><td><b>1/12/43</b></td><td><b>15/12/43</b></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><b>SYRIA</b></td><td><b>16/12/43</b></td><td><b>8/7/44</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>D.D. BFN.</b></td><td><b>13.8.44</b> [sic — 13.8.45]</td><td><b>24.8.44</b> [sic — 24.8.45]</td><td><b>SAMC TRANSIT CAMP</b></td><td><b>EGYPT</b></td><td><b>9/7/44</b></td><td><b>8/8/44</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>24.8.45 Demob</b> (added below table)</td><td></td><td></td><td><b>PTO</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Margin, left, in ink: <b>Disch.</b> and a struck symbol.</p>\n<p>Were you wounded in action <b>No</b> Where — When —<br>Were you evacuated from a battle area because of wounds, if so, give details:— —<br>If, during your military or other service, you won an Honour or Decoration or have been Mentioned in Despatches, state award received —<br>Were you at any time a prisoner of war, if so, state dates from — to — Country —</p>\n<p><b>C.</b> If you served during the war, or are still serving in a PART TIME UNIT, give details hereunder:—<br>Name of part time unit <b>4th Bde. Signal Coy.</b> Regtl. No. (part time) <b>3038</b><br>Date of attestation <b>App. 1/6/39</b> Date and place of discharge <b>?</b><br>If still serving in a part-time capacity, state name of unit —</p>\n<p><b>D.</b> Ex-members of the NATIVE MILITARY CORPS must state here the name and address of their Native Commissioner [blank]</p>\n<p><b>E.</b> STATEMENT BY APPLICANT.<br>I have already received the ribbons of the undermentioned awards. These ribbons were supplied to me by:—<br><b>Africa Star + 8th Army Clasp : 10/11 FLD. AMB. SAMC.</b><br><b>Africa Service : 140 Mil. Hosp. BFN.</b></p>\n<p>(Delete those not applicable) { AFRICA STAR. <b>X</b> / <s>1939-45 STAR.</s> [struck] / AFRICA SERVICE MEDAL. }</p>\n<p>Signature of Applicant <b>A M Lapinsky</b> Date <b>26/9/45</b></p>\n<p>PLEASE READ NOTES OVERLEAF.</p>"},{"id":"P17","title":"Form D.D. 873 — reverse (Notes and fold panel)","html":"<p>NOTES.<br>1. Fill in form in block letters (except your signature).<br>2. Do NOT send reminders, it may be sometime before your ribbons are despatched.<br>3. Your statement will be carefully checked. Incorrect information will delay your claim.<br>4. Do not apply for individual medals. Your service will be reviewed and the ribbons you are entitled to receive will be forwarded to you as soon as possible.<br>5. Ex-members of the Women's Auxiliary Defence Corps should mention any change of name caused by marriage or re-marriage during the period of military service.<br>6. If you have rendered both PART time and FULL time service in the U.D.F. since 6.9.39, you must complete Section \"C\" in addition to Section B.<br>7. Be sure that your regimental number is CORRECTLY quoted. If you are unable to remember exact dates insert the word \"approximately\" where necessary.<br>8. Do NOT send in your \"Discharge Certificate\" or any other documents with this application.<br>9. Post this form to A.G., WAR RECORDS, HAMILTON STREET, PRETORIA.<br>10. Fold the form as indicated on back hereof to avoid use of envelopes.</p>\n<p>FIRST FOLD. / FOURTH FOLD. / THIRD FOLD. / SECOND FOLD. / INSERT THIS FLAP.<br><b>O.H.M.S.</b> A.G. (WAR RECORDS), HAMILTON STREET, PRETORIA. <span class=\"stamp\">POSTMARK: … OCT 1945 … PM</span></p>\n<p>Pencil notes (written upside-down in the flap panel, clerk's check of the applicant's dates):<br><b>Emb Dbn 9.6.41</b><br><b>Dis Emb 21.6.41</b><br><b>Empl[aned] for Union 6.8.44</b><br><b>Emplaned [?] … E</b> [illegible]<br><b>19/1 … [illegible]</b><br><b>… [illegible]</b></p><h4>Pencil notes on the fold panel (read after rotating 180°)</h4><p><b>Emb Dbn 9.6.41</b><br><b>Dis Suez 21.6.41</b><br><b>Empl for Union 6.8.44</b><br><b>Eligible for 8</b> [= 8th Army clasp] <b>10/11 Fld Amb</b><br><b>Verified as amended</b> [signature] <b>O.R. Sward</b> [?]</p>"},{"id":"P18","title":"Annexure to Form D.D. 873 (Discharged Personnel) — copy 1","html":"<p>G.P.-S.40434—1945-6—300,000. S.<br><b>ANNEXURE TO FORM D.D. 873. (DISCHARGED PERSONNEL.)</b><br>REGISTRATION No. <b>3501/3550.</b><br>NOTE. { Original to be forwarded to A.G., War Records. / Duplicate to be retained at verification point.</p>\n<p>Regimental No. <b>176073V</b> Name (Mr., Mrs., Miss) <b>L/Cpl A.M. LAPINSKY</b><br>Unit or Corps <b>SAMC</b> A.G. Authority <b>WR 176073V/22</b></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Awards Provisionally Approved.</th><th>Verified by.</th><th>Checked by.</th><th>Ribbons Despatched by.</th><th>Date.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1939-45 STAR <b>✓</b></td><td><b>W Smart</b> [?]</td><td><b>J. Delmy</b> [?]</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>ATLANTIC STAR</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><s>AIR CREW EUROPE STAR</s></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>AFRICA STAR <b>+ 8 Army Clasp</b> <b>✓</b></td><td><b>W Smart</b></td><td><b>J. Delmy</b></td><td><b>previously awarded.</b></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><s>PACIFIC STAR</s></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><s>BURMA STAR</s></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><s>ITALY STAR</s></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><s>FRANCE AND GERMANY STAR</s></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DEFENCE MEDAL BRITISH <b>✓</b></td><td><b>W Smart</b></td><td><b>J. Delmy</b></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(Delete those not applicable.)<br>Details of forfeiture (if any) [blank]<br>Entered in Control Register by <b>H de Vrye</b> [?] Date <b>4/12/45</b></p>"},{"id":"P19","title":"Annexure to Form D.D. 873 — copy 2, with ribbon-issue letter","html":"<p>(Same printed form as P-18, carbon/duplicate; entries identical except as noted.)</p>\n<p>REGISTRATION No. <b>3501/3550.</b><br>Regimental No. <b>176073V</b> Name <b>L/Cpl A.M. LAPINSKY</b> Unit or Corps <b>SAMC</b> A.G. Authority <b>WR 176073V/22</b></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Awards Provisionally Approved.</th><th>Verified by.</th><th>Checked by.</th><th>Ribbons Despatched by.</th><th>Date.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1939-45 STAR <b>✓</b></td><td><b>W Smart</b></td><td><b>J. Delmy</b></td><td><b>JSE</b> [initials]</td><td><b>21/1/46</b></td></tr><tr><td>AFRICA STAR <b>+ 8 Army Clasp</b></td><td><b>W Smart</b></td><td><b>J. Delmy</b></td><td><b>previously awarded</b></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DEFENCE MEDAL BRITISH <b>✓</b></td><td><b>W Smart</b></td><td><b>J. Delmy</b></td><td><b>JE</b> [initials]</td><td><b>21/1/46</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Entered in Control Register by <b>H de Vrye</b> [?] Date <b>4/12/45</b></p>\n<h4>(perforation)</h4>\n<p>To <b>MR A.M. LAPINSKY, 14A WAVERLEY RD, BLOEMFONTEIN.</b><br>A.G. War Records, Hamilton Street, Pretoria.</p>\n<p>DEAR SIR/MADAM,<br>You have provisionally qualified to receive the undermentioned awards, the ribbons of which are attached hereto:—<br><b>1939 - 45 STAR</b><br><b>AFRICA STAR + 8 ARMY CLASP</b><br><b>DEFENCE MEDAL BRITISH</b></p>\n<p>These awards are subject to final confirmation at a later date and subject to forfeiture and/or restoration in terms of the British Army Council Instruction No. A.C.I. 1452 of 31st. March, 1945.</p>\n<p>Yours Faithfully, [signature illegible] Col. Officer in Charge, War Records.</p>\n<p>OFFICIAL STAMP: <code>[STAMP, oval:] ADJUTANT-GENERAL · HAMILTON STREET · 22-11-1945 · PRETORIA · WAR RECORDS</code> Adjutant-General. Authority for Issue: <b>WR 176073V/22</b></p>\n<p><code>[BOX:] THIS DOCUMENT IS NOT VALID UNLESS IT BEARS THE OFFICIAL STAMP OF THE ADJUTANT-GENERAL AND IS SIGNED BY THE RESPONSIBLE OFFICER.</code></p>\n<p>Bottom margin, pencil: <b>Ribbon of the Africa Star + 8 Army clasp previously issued</b></p>"},{"id":"P20","title":"D.D. 732 — Record Card (front), second copy (white card)","html":"<p>(Red diagonal cancellation line. Pencil <b>G</b> [?] top left; red pencil <b>F</b> [?] and pencil <b>X4</b> top centre.)</p>\n<p>D.D. 732.<br>CARD No / No. van KAART: — REGTL. No. / Regtsno. <b>176073</b></p>\n<p>A. — Surname (a) / Van <b>LAPINSKY</b><br>Christian Names (a) / Voorname <b>AUBREY MITCHELL</b><br>Rank (b) / Rang: pencil <s><b>Pte</b></s> <b>T/L/Cpl</b> · Unit (b) / Eenheid: pencil <b>10/11 FD. AMB.</b><br>Date of Birth / Datum van geboorte <b>15-12-1918</b><br>Religious Denomination / Kerkverband <b>JEW</b><br>Next of Kin / Naasbestaande — Relationship / Verwantskap <b>FATHER</b> · Name / Naam <b>MR NATHAN LAPINSKY</b> · Address / Adres <b>24 ALEXANDRA AVENUE, BLOEMFONTEIN.</b></p>\n<p>To be completed in RED INK. / Moet met ROOI INK ingevul word.<br>B. — Date record returned O. i/c War Records / Datum wanneer teruggestuur na die offisier vir oorlogsregisters: <span class=\"stamp\">STAMP: 16-8-1944</span> <code>[STAMP:] OFFICER i/c RECORDS, SECT. \"G\" · 2nd Echelon, U.D.F., M.E.F.</code> [signature] <b>Brownbill</b> [?] <b>Captain</b><br>Reason / Rede: red ink capitals <b>EMPLANED FOR UNION ON HOME EXCHANGE</b><br>(a) To be entered in BLOCK CAPITALS. / Most in DRUKKAPITALE ingeskryf word. (b) To be entered in black pencil. / Moet met swart potlood ingeskryf word.</p>"},{"id":"P21","title":"D.D. 732 — Record of Service / Diensstaat (reverse of P-20)","html":"<p>RECORD OF SERVICE. — DIENSSTAAT.<br>(Entries in pencil; the two heavier entries — 25 Jan 43 and 9 July 44/6 Aug 44 — in black ink. Some pencil lines are badly faded; readings below were obtained from contrast-enhanced 300 dpi crops and cross-checked against P-3 and S-2, which carry the same entries.)</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Date / Datum</th><th>Nature of Casualty / Aard van verlies</th><th>Unit</th><th>Reference / Verwysing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>23 July 41</b> (arrowed, written above the first rule, i.e. inserted later)</td><td><b>Granted 4d p.d. Annual Incr.</b></td><td><b>10/11 F.A.</b></td><td><b>P.II O 7 : 23 FEB 42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>21 June 41</b></td><td><b>Disembarked Suez</b></td><td></td><td><b>P.II O/1 30-6-41</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>6.2.42 – 13.2.42</b></td><td><b>Granted local leave + 2/- p.d. Ration allce.</b></td><td></td><td><b>7 23-2-42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>3 July 42</b></td><td><b>Off strength + placed on X 4 (G/L P.II O 27 d/d 13/7/42)</b></td><td><b>16 F.A.</b></td><td><b>P.II O. 24 13.7.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>1-8-42</b></td><td><b>Detached to 10/11 Fd Amb.</b></td><td><b>G/L.</b></td><td><b>31 10-8-42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>2.9.42</b></td><td><b>On Posting to 10/11 F.Amb fm SAMC G/L (10/11 F.A. 33/42)</b></td><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>35 7.9.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>11.9.42 to 24.9.42</b></td><td><b>Granted leave + 2/- p.d. ration allce.</b></td><td><b>10/11 F.A.</b></td><td><b>35 21.9.42</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>19.10.42</b> (faded)</td><td><b>Promoted T/L/Cpl.</b></td><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>40. 26.10.42.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>23.7.42</b> (faded)</td><td><b>Granted 2nd annual increment of 4d p.d.</b></td><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>44. 23.11.42.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>25 Jan 43</b> (ink)</td><td><b>Admit to hosp. — on X2 list</b></td><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>6 – 8/2/43</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>11 Feb 43</b> (faded)</td><td><b>Rejoined Unit. Off X2 list.</b></td><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>8. 22 Feb 43.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>9 July 44</b></td><td><b>Placed on S.A.M.C. Gen list (G.L. O/29/44)</b></td><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>O/29/44. 17/7/44.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>6 Aug 44</b> (ink)</td><td><b>Emplaned for Union on Home Exch.</b></td><td><b>SAMC GL</b></td><td><b>O/33: 14 Aug 44</b> }</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Footer: 1115 / P.M.E.O. / 60,000 / 6/41</p>"},{"id":"S01","title":"Card 1: front (bottom half) and \"Offences\" page (top half)","html":"<p>Top half: <b>OFFENCES.</b> — ruled page, no entries.</p>\n<p>Bottom half (card front):<br>G.P.-S.11898—1940—200,000. S. · D.D. 293. (W.R. 6.) · <code>[STAMP, purple:] ANYWHERE</code> · faint pencil top right <b>Ha… file</b> [?]</p>\n<p>Regt. No. <b>176073</b> + red <b>V</b> · Surname <b>LAPINSKY.</b><br>Christian Names <b>Aubrey Mitchell</b><br>Next of kin (Relationship) <b>Father.</b> Name <b>Mr. N. Lapinsky</b><br>Address <b>24 Alexandra Ave, Bloemfontein.</b> (red <b>S</b> [?] after the town)<br>Age <b>21.</b> (written above the line) <b>15.12.18</b> Religion <b>Jewish.</b> Occupation [blank]<br>Postings <b>Pte. 16th Fld. Amb. S.A.M.C. 23.7.40.</b><br>(second line, red ink) <b>176073 Pte 16th Fld. Amb. S.A.M.C. 12.12.40</b><br>Moves <b>Emb Durban for Mid East 9.6.41, per SS. Ile de France, with 16 Fld Amb (KR 218).</b><br><b>Dis Emb at Suez 21.6.41 (FO 1/41/413 ME)</b><br><b>Att 10/11 Fld Amb from SAMC \"G\" List <s>31/7/42</s> 1/8/42</b> (correction written above) <b>(FO 29/42/260 ME)</b> [with <b>F.O. 31/42/367 M.E.</b> written in small above] <b>posted to 10/11 Fd Amb from S.A.M.C 2/9/42 (FO 33/42/260 ME) placed on X2 list adm to hosp. 25/1/43 (FO 6/43/260 ME) Struck off X2 List Disch. hosp 11/2/43 (FO 8/43/260 ME) On strength SAMC Gen list from 16 Fd Amb 3/7/42 (FO 24/42/367 ME)</b> [with <b>(FO 24/42/413 ME)</b> written in small above]<br>Transfers [blank]</p>"},{"id":"S02","title":"Card 1: inside pages (Promotions / Battle Casualties / Miscellaneous, and Hospital Record)","html":"<p>D.D. 293. (W.R. 6.)</p>\n<p>Promotions <b>T/L/Cpl w.e.f. 19/10/42 (FO 40/42/260 ME) Granted 4 p.d. annual inc. on completion of 24 months service Basic Rate of Pay inc. to 4/2 23/7/42 (FO 44/42/260 ME)</b></p>\n<p>Battle Casualties [blank]</p>\n<p>Miscellaneous <b>Granted 2/- p.d. R/A 11/9/42 – 24/9/42 (FO 35/42/260 ME) leave 11/9/42 – 24/9/42 (FO 35/42/260 ME) Granted local leave: 6/2/42 – 13/2/42 (FO 7/42/413 ME)</b> (last reference runs off the right edge)</p>\n<p><b>HOSPITAL RECORD.</b></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Date.</th><th>Disability, Casualty, etc. — Nature.</th><th>Place.</th><th>Hospitals.</th><th>Remarks, References.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>(FO 6/43/260 ME) 25/1/43</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(No other entries.)</p>"},{"id":"S03","title":"Card 2: front (bottom half) and Record of Service page (top half, blank)","html":"<p>Top half: <b>RECORD OF SERVICE.</b> — Date / Particulars / Reference — no entries.</p>\n<p>Bottom half: G.P.-S.38311—1942-3—50,000. S. · <b>Card 2</b> · D.D. 293. (W R. 6.)<br>Block No. <b>176073.</b> Surname <b>L A P I N S K Y.</b> Christian names <b>Aubrey, Mitchell,</b><br>Date of Birth / Occupation / Height / Distinctive Marks / Religion / Complexion / Eyes / Hair / Medical Category / Posting / Next-of-Kin / Other persons to be notified — all blank.</p>"},{"id":"S04","title":"Card 2: Record of Service (1942–1945)","html":"<p>RECORD OF SERVICE.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Date.</th><th>Particulars.</th><th>Reference.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>2.9.42.</b></td><td><b>Off strength S.A.M.C. on posting to 10/11 Fld. Amb.</b></td><td><b>(FO 35/42/367 ME)</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>13-6-43.</b></td><td><b>10/11 Fld. Ambulance (V) S.A.M.C. M.E.</b></td><td><b>D.D. 88. B.R.</b> [?]</td></tr><tr><td><b>9.7.44</b></td><td><b>off str SAMC 10/11 Fld Ambu. (V) SAMC, placed on SAMC G/List</b></td><td><b>FO 29-44-595 ME</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>9/7/44</b></td><td><b>On Str SAMC G/List from 10/11 (SA) Fd. Amb</b></td><td><b>FO 29/44/585 ME</b> [?]</td></tr><tr><td><b>8/8/44</b></td><td><b>On Str Base depot V/Hoogte ex ME by air (cat A)</b></td><td><b>FO 32/44/478</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>9/8/44</b></td><td><b>Off Str Base depot V/Hoogte to SAM TC S/Water</b></td><td><b>FO 32/44/478</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>6/8/44</b></td><td><b>Emplaned for Union</b></td><td><b>FO 33/44/585 ME</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>9.9.44.</b></td><td><b>On Str S.A.M.C. T/C. S/Water ex U.B.D. V/Hoogte.</b></td><td><b>UO 90/44/593.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>14-10-44.</b></td><td><b>On Str 140 Mil Hosp Tempe ex M.T.C. S/Water</b></td><td><b>UO 28/44/1572.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>13-10-44</b></td><td><b>Off Str S.A.M.C. T/C Z/water. Post. to Mil. Hosp. Tempe</b></td><td><b>U.O. 97/44/593.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>31-10-44</b></td><td><b>Adm to Hosp</b></td><td><b>UO 31/44/1572</b> [?]</td></tr><tr><td>(red ink)</td><td><b>Awarded Africa Service Medal</b></td><td><b>UO 34/44/1572.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>19.12.[44]</b></td><td><b>Cat C</b></td><td><b>D D Med 25</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>[2?]6.12.44.</b></td><td><b>Disch. from Hosp</b></td><td><b>UO 57.44.1572</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>1.1.45.</b></td><td><b>Prom. from L/Cpl to T/Cpl. (Cat. C)</b></td><td><b>UO 11/45/1572.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>13.8.45.</b></td><td><b>Off Str 140 MH Bloemfontein to O.C. Disp Dept Tempe</b></td><td><b>UO 32/45/1572</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>14.8.45</b></td><td><b>On Str Disp Depot Tempe Bloemfontein from 140 Mil Hosp. S.A.M.C. Tempe</b></td><td><b>UO 57/45/1765</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(Lower half of the opening is blank ruled lines; the fold is heavily foxed/stained.)</p>"},{"id":"S05","title":"Card 3 (discharge card): front (bottom half) and blank Record of Service (top half)","html":"<p>Top half: <b>RECORD OF SERVICE.</b> — no entries.</p>\n<p>Bottom half: G.P.-S.42297—1943-4—50,000. S. · <code>[STAMP, purple:] ANYWHERE</code> · D.D. 293. (W.R. 6.)<br>Block No. <b>176073</b> + red <b>V</b> · Surname <b>LAPINSKY</b> · Christian names <b>Aubrey, Mitchell.</b><br>Date of Birth <b>21.</b> (age) <b>15/12/18</b> Occupation <b>·</b> Height [blank]<br>Distinctive Marks [blank] Religion <b>Jewish.</b><br>Complexion / Eyes / Hair [blank] · <code>[STAMP, purple:] DISCHARGE authorised</code> <b>17/7/45</b> (red)<br>Medical Category [blank]<br>Posting <b>Pte 16 Fld Amb. S.A.M.C. 23/7/40</b><br>Next-of-Kin (relationship, name, address) <s><b>Father. Mr N. Lapinsky 24 Alexandra Ave Bloemfontein.</b></s> [struck] <b>WIFE, (19:8:44.)</b><br><b>MRS A. LAPINSKY 14A WAVERLEY ROAD BLOEMFONTEIN.. UO 96/44/593.</b></p>\n<p>(Lower section, over the \"Other persons to be notified\" line — medal entitlement, in red ink, bracketed:)</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Medals</th><th>Despatch record</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>1939-45 Star</b></td><td><b>Serial 6867.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>Africa Star</b></td><td><b>Desp: 1/3/57.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>Defence Medal (British)</b></td><td><b>Reg: No: 41/6991.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>The War Medal 1939-45</b></td><td><b>Book 15.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>Africa Service Medal</b></td><td><b>Page 376.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>8th Army Clasp.</b></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><code>[STAMP, purple:] DISCHARGED · C.G. &amp; A.C.F. REGULATIONS · Chapter IV., Section 30 (</code> <b>E</b> <code>) · DATE</code> <b>24/8/45 (UO 64/45/1765 — 27/8/45).</b> (red)</p>"},{"id":"S06","title":"Card 3: Record of Service, 1940–1941","html":"<p><b>1940</b> · RECORD OF SERVICE.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Date.</th><th>Particulars.</th><th>Reference.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>No date</b></td><td><b>Posted to 16 Fld Amb ex R.T.C.</b></td><td><b>U.O. 5/40/273</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>\"</b></td><td><b>Off Str. R.T.C. to 16 Fld. Amb.</b></td><td><b>UO 47/40/274.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>25/7/40</b></td><td><b>Drafted into R.T.C. (Recruit)</b></td><td><b>UO 36/40/274.</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>No date</b></td><td><b>On Str 16 Fld Amb. Ex R.T.C</b></td><td><b>UO 49.40.245</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>1941</b></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Date.</th><th>Particulars.</th><th>Reference.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>1.2.41.</b></td><td><b>Sick Leave to 6.2.41</b></td><td><b>UO 33/41/273.</b></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>(Remaining lines blank; fold heavily foxed.)</p>"}],"glossary":[{"a":"A.C.F.","conf":true,"e":"Active Citizen Force (the part-time/volunteer force of the UDF)"},{"a":"A.G.","conf":true,"e":"Adjutant-General"},{"a":"A.G.W.R. / WR","conf":true,"e":"Adjutant-General War Records / War Records (the Pretoria records office)"},{"a":"Adm","conf":false,"e":"Admitted (to hospital)"},{"a":"Allce","conf":false,"e":"Allowance"},{"a":"Amb / Fd Amb / Fld Amb","conf":true,"e":"(Field) Ambulance — a mobile medical unit supporting a brigade"},{"a":"Amnd","conf":false,"e":"Amended"},{"a":"Att","conf":true,"e":"Attached"},{"a":"A.W.O.L.","conf":true,"e":"Absent Without Leave"},{"a":"B.D. / U.B.D.","conf":true,"e":"Base Depot / Union Base Depot (Voortrekkerhoogte)"},{"a":"Bde","conf":false,"e":"Brigade"},{"a":"Bfn / BFN","conf":false,"e":"Bloemfontein"},{"a":"Capt","conf":false,"e":"Captain"},{"a":"Cat (A/C)","conf":false,"e":"Medical category (A = fit for general service; C = fit for home/base duties only)"},{"a":"C.C.S.","conf":true,"e":"Casualty Clearing Station"},{"a":"C.C.S.C.A.","conf":false,"e":"Civilian Clothing and Cash Allowance (the £30 discharge grant)"},{"a":"C.G. & A.C.F. Regs","conf":false,"e":"Coast Garrison and Active Citizen Force Regulations"},{"a":"Cpl","conf":true,"e":"Corporal"},{"a":"D.D.","conf":true,"e":"Defence Document (form series, e.g. D.D. 88B, D.D. 293, D.D. 732, D.D. 872, D.D. 873)"},{"a":"D.D. BFN / Disp Depot","conf":false,"e":"Dispersal Depot, Bloemfontein (Tempe)"},{"a":"D.G.D.","conf":true,"e":"Director-General of Dispersals (hence Form DGD 15(A), D.G.D. III)"},{"a":"Demob","conf":true,"e":"Demobilisation"},{"a":"Dis Emb / Disemb","conf":false,"e":"Disembarked"},{"a":"Disch","conf":false,"e":"Discharged"},{"a":"D.N.E.A.S.","conf":true,"e":"Director Non-European Army Services"},{"a":"D.S.D.C.","conf":false,"e":"Demobilisation (Dispersal) Sub-Directorate/Committee, Bloemfontein — the body that handled post-discharge benefit applications"},{"a":"Ech / 2nd Echelon","conf":true,"e":"Echelon — 2nd Echelon was the records office of a force in the field (here \"2nd Echelon, U.D.F., M.E.F.\")"},{"a":"Emb","conf":true,"e":"Embarked"},{"a":"Emplaned","conf":false,"e":"Boarded an aircraft"},{"a":"F.A.","conf":false,"e":"Field Ambulance (also Field Allowance †, but in this file always the unit)"},{"a":"FO","conf":true,"e":"Force Order (WWII) — the UDF in the Middle East's published orders; e.g. \"FO 24/42/367 ME\" = Force Order no. 24 of 1942, para. 367, Middle East"},{"a":"G.C. Badges","conf":false,"e":"Good Conduct badges"},{"a":"Gen List / G List / G/L / \"G\" List","conf":true,"e":"General List (WWII) — holding list for men not on the strength of a specific unit"},{"a":"G.P.-S.","conf":true,"e":"Government Printer – Staatsdrukker (form printing code)"},{"a":"Hosp","conf":false,"e":"Hospital"},{"a":"Incr / Inc","conf":false,"e":"Increment (of pay)"},{"a":"KR 218","conf":false,"e":"King's Regulations para. 218 (authority cited for the embarkation)"},{"a":"L/Cpl","conf":false,"e":"Lance-Corporal"},{"a":"L.W.O.P.","conf":true,"e":"Leave Without Pay"},{"a":"M.D.C.","conf":true,"e":"Military Discipline Code (hence M.D.C. 46 conduct sheet)"},{"a":"ME / M.E.F.","conf":true,"e":"Middle East / Middle East Forces"},{"a":"Med Cat","conf":false,"e":"Medical Category"},{"a":"M.H. / Mil Hosp","conf":false,"e":"Military Hospital"},{"a":"M.T.C.","conf":false,"e":"(SAMC) Training Centre — the Sonderwater medical training centre (written \"T/C\", \"T.C.\", \"M.T.C.\")"},{"a":"O.C.","conf":true,"e":"Officer Commanding"},{"a":"O. i/c","conf":true,"e":"Officer in charge"},{"a":"O.H.M.S.","conf":false,"e":"On His Majesty's Service"},{"a":"p.d.","conf":false,"e":"per diem (per day)"},{"a":"P.I. / P.II O / P.T. II O / Pt II O","conf":false,"e":"Part II Orders — the unit's daily personnel orders, the authority for each record entry"},{"a":"P.M.E.J. / P.M.E.O.","conf":false,"e":"Printing codes on D.D. 732 cards (Printer, Middle East …)"},{"a":"P.O.W.","conf":false,"e":"Prisoner of War"},{"a":"Pte","conf":true,"e":"Private"},{"a":"R.A. / R/A","conf":true,"e":"Ration Allowance"},{"a":"Regtl. No.","conf":false,"e":"Regimental Number"},{"a":"R.O.","conf":false,"e":"Routine Order † / Release Order"},{"a":"R.S.P.","conf":true,"e":"Release from Service Period"},{"a":"R.T.C.","conf":false,"e":"Recruit Training Centre"},{"a":"S.A.C.S.","conf":true,"e":"South African Corps of Signals (his pre-war part-time corps)"},{"a":"S.A.M.C.","conf":true,"e":"South African Medical Corps"},{"a":"Str / Sts","conf":false,"e":"Strength (on/off strength of a unit)"},{"a":"S/Water, Z/water","conf":false,"e":"Sonderwater (Zonderwater), the camp near Cullinan"},{"a":"T/ (T/L/Cpl, T/Cpl)","conf":true,"e":"Temporary (rank)"},{"a":"T/C, T.C.","conf":true,"e":"Training Centre"},{"a":"U.D.F.","conf":true,"e":"Union Defence Force"},{"a":"UO","conf":true,"e":"Unit Order (the Union-side equivalent of a Force Order; e.g. \"UO 28/44/1572\")"},{"a":"(V)","conf":false,"e":"suffix on \"10/11 Field Ambulance (V)\" — not in the booklet; most likely \"Volunteer\" (see Timeline-Research.md)"},{"a":"V (after regtl. no.)","conf":false,"e":"the volunteer suffix given to UDF men who took the oath to serve outside the Union (\"ANYWHERE\" stamp)"},{"a":"V/Hoogte","conf":true,"e":"Voortrekkerhoogte (formerly Roberts Heights), Pretoria"},{"a":"w.e.f.","conf":false,"e":"with effect from"},{"a":"WM","conf":false,"e":"War Measure (e.g. \"WM 58/43\" — the Government War Measures governing demobilisation)"},{"a":"WR (7)","conf":false,"e":"War Records section 7 (authority reference for discharge)"},{"a":"X2 list / X4 list","conf":false,"e":"\"X\" lists — categories of men temporarily off unit strength (X2 = in hospital; X4 = in transit/reinforcement pool)"}]};